# NestJS Patterns

## Modules

- Use `@Module()` with explicit imports/exports
- Keep modules focused; avoid god-modules
- Feature modules import only what they need

## Dependency Injection

- Inject via constructor; prefer `@Injectable()` services
- Use `forRoot()` / `forFeature()` for ConfigModule, database modules
- Avoid circular dependencies — extract shared code to separate modules

## Guards

- `JwtAuthGuard` — protect routes that require auth
- `TenantGuard` — compare `param.companyId` with `activeCompanyId` from JWT; return 403 on mismatch
- Guards run before handlers; do not pass `param.companyId` into services — always use `activeCompanyId` from JWT

## Exception Filters

- Use NestJS built-in exceptions (e.g. `UnauthorizedException`, `ForbiddenException`)
- Custom filters for consistent error response format
- 403 for tenant mismatch; 401 for auth failures
